{
  "kanda": "bala",
  "sarga": 25,
  "title": "The legend of Tataka, continued",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga25/balasans25.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga25/balaitrans25.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Sage Vishvamitra narrates the birth, marriage and curse of demoness Tataka, and bids Rama to eliminate her menace without any hesitation of killing a female, for she is atrocious towards the society."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकिरामायणे आदिकाव्ये बालकाण्डे पंचविंशः सर्गः ||",
    "This is a much discussed topic in Ramayana. Rama's adventures start with the killing of a female. While scriptures say that killing a female is sinful, is this killing of a female righteous or wrongful is the topic for discussion. It is said in answer that there is no harm to dharma since unrighteousness is eliminable though existing in the form of a female.duṣṭastrīvadhe doṣo nāstīti śāstreṇa na anyena - dharmākūtam ||",
    "And ViShNu Purana says that eliminating one evildoer for the sake of many innocent is neither sin nor a crime of course, to the kings and rulers: yasmin atra nidhanam prāpte duṣṭakāriṇi | bahūnām bhavati kṣemaḥ tasya puṇyaprado vadhaḥ || - viṣṇu purāna 1-13-73-74",
    "For the sake many, that too defenceless rural people, it is the duty of the king to eliminate whether it is a male or a female if involved in atrocities: dharmārthapūrvakam tāṭakāvadhe doṣo nāsti - -- puṇyam eva bhaviṣyati iti tātparyeṇa maharṣiviśvāmitreṇa uktam | idānīmtanairapi bahūnām kṣemārtham ekasya hanane doṣo nāsti iti jñeyam | viśeṣitaḥ rājñā janapadarakṣaṇadīkṣitena avadhyavadho api kartavyaḥ ityapi sūcitam || --- dharmākūtam",
    "Thus, this is the 25th chapter in Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1.25.1",
      "label": "1.25.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "अथ तस्याप्रमेयस्य मुनेर्वचनमुत्तमम् |\nश्रुत्वा पुरुषशार्दूलः प्रत्युवाच शुभां गिरम्",
      "iast": "atha tasya aprameyasya muner vacanam uttamam |\nśrutvā puruṣa śārdūlaḥ pratyuvāca śubhām giram",
