      "devanagari": "इत्युक्तं वचनं श्रुत्वा राघवस्यामितोजसा |\nहर्षयन् श्लक्ष्णया वाचा सलक्ष्मणमरिन्दमम्\nविश्वामित्रोऽब्रवीद्वाक्यं शृणु येन बलोत्कटा |\nवरदानकृतं वीर्यं धारयत्यबला बलम्",
      "iast": "iti ukta,m vacanam śrutvā rāghavasya amita ojasā |\nharṣayan ślakśṇayā vacā sa lakśmaṇam arindamam\nviśvāmitro'bravīt vākyam śṛṇu yena balotkaṭā |\nvara dāna kṛtam vīryam dhārayati abalā balam",
      "translation": "On hearing the sentence of Raghava with illimitable dynamism, Vishvamitra said this sentence to the enemy subduer Rama along with Lakshmana, cheering them up with his pleasant words, \"Listen by which a female became outstanding by her strength... she assumes strength by the bestowal of a boon.",
