          "iast": "kartavyam",
          "devanagari": "कर्तव्यं",
          "meaning": "is to be done - effectuated.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 13
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.25.18",
      "label": "1.25.18",
      "numbers": [
        18
      ],
      "devanagari": "नृशंसमनृशंसं वा प्रजारक्षणकारणात् |\nपातकं वा सदोषं वा कर्तव्यं रक्षता सदा",
      "iast": "nṛśaṃsam anṛśaṃsam vā prajā rakśaṇa kāraṇāt |\npātakam vā sadoṣam vā kartavyam rakśatā sadā",
      "translation": "\"For the reason of protecting people, a protector always has to execute such deed, either it is ruthless or humane, sinful or vilifying.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "rakshata",
          "iast": "rakśata",
          "devanagari": "रक्शत",
          "meaning": "[to a king] who is protector [of subjects]",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
